<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:50Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US, Russia and Ukraine to restart talks in Abu Dhabi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf6248b287a85a13b3a002610149b6f5c7bf27079272ee8e782d17272bba6f59</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T07:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-russia-and-ukraine-to-restart-talks-in-abu-dhabi/live-79906232--4a61d4371146.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-russia-and-ukraine-to-restart-talks-in-abu-dhabi/live-79906232?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Peace talks between Russia, Ukraine and the US are getting underway in the United Arab Emirates. It is the first such meeting since February. DW has the latest updates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: New Delhi ready to mediate Black Sea food corridors, says Ukraine's Zelenskyy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f77af9af893542b42ca3bc5bec0ae83bd20d488ad6b3c6793565bd5701cb8d2e</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-ready-to-mediate-black-sea-food-corridors-says-ukraine-s-zelenskyy/live-79906023--cfcf53dfd0a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-ready-to-mediate-black-sea-food-corridors-says-ukraine-s-zelenskyy/live-79906023?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said he discussed establishing "food corridors" in the Black Sea in a phone call with Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why malnutrition can go unnoticed, and what that means for our health</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8f3a70d348d26e6d96222a82491f12fe33fae47bb914997d9c7a8ea978379e6</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-malnutrition-can-go-unnoticed-and-what-that-means-for-our-health/a-79871016--a7247c0af1e5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-malnutrition-can-go-unnoticed-and-what-that-means-for-our-health/a-79871016?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 2 billion people worldwide suffer from nutrient deficiencies, most of them in the Global South. The health consequences can be devastating.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Australia to introduce mandatory AI safeguards</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f579515f8522b8e995e2af1858f70be03f778f4e012683ac7a66b64e9f736ecf</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T04:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australia-to-introduce-mandatory-ai-safeguards/a-79906006--f7d003a54254.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australia-to-introduce-mandatory-ai-safeguards/a-79906006?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Australian government's decision to establish an AI safety regulator comes after an OpenAI agent accessed a government medical statistics portal without authorization.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war oil shock drives dip in global emissions, study shows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6f6b03e2fbae5ba3209dad8abb1714e921c69013db16847a2e0014612cc16f9</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T03:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-oil-shock-drives-dip-in-global-emissions-study-shows/a-79905937--fec20d5dba18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-oil-shock-drives-dip-in-global-emissions-study-shows/a-79905937?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Global carbon emissions are expected to fall slightly in 2026, but not because of major progress on climate action. Instead, it's high energy prices following the US attack on Iran that's driving the trend.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia shareholders sue Jensen Huang over alleged spy ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b95fe6553f2aedc173455bb5e3aab74353a3e23ddf1d22379dc5844cc37cffe</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T23:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-shareholders-sue-jensen-huang-over-alleged-spy-ties/a-79905809--f4200acf2967.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-shareholders-sue-jensen-huang-over-alleged-spy-ties/a-79905809?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia shareholders have sued the chipmaker and its CEO, Jensen Huang, over his alleged ties to a suspected Chinese spy. The case adds to scrutiny over whether sensitive information at the AI giant was compromised.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>New trilateral talks on Ukraine war in Abu Dhabi: What to expect?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c91c39fcd5db35f2f7fc2f699623a9c750d8b9a7f52fc2fcaee5b5dbec48fd8d</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T23:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-trilateral-talks-on-ukraine-war-in-abu-dhabi-what-to-expect/a-79905734--3c6da76b72e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-trilateral-talks-on-ukraine-war-in-abu-dhabi-what-to-expect/a-79905734?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian and Russian representatives last met in February for talks on ending the war, but the same sticking points remain. Ukraine continues to demand security guarantees, which is a non-starter for Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Skydance replaces James Gunn and Peter Safran as DC Studios chiefs following Warner Bros. takeover</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1de4a9cc55f154895034a457fc3f1243a67d037dbb771935c926388a12d76e1</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/skydance-replaces-james-gunn-and-peter-safran-as-dc-studios-chiefs-following-warner-bros-takeover/a-79904972--485cbd8afddc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/skydance-replaces-james-gunn-and-peter-safran-as-dc-studios-chiefs-following-warner-bros-takeover/a-79904972?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In another major shake-up for the DC Studios, Skydance is replacing Hollywood director James Gunn and producer Peter Safran with a former Marvel executive.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US Pentagon chief Hegseth faces impeachment push over Iran war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adccb6188bb4c1c0d474bb3dc4966ef1bc12e73e1655570c7a90e15786c1d243</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:32:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-pentagon-chief-hegseth-faces-impeachment-push-over-iran-war/a-79905323--5b9e4c4948cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-pentagon-chief-hegseth-faces-impeachment-push-over-iran-war/a-79905323?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trump critic Thomas Massie is calling for a vote to impeach Pentagon chief Pete Hegseth, accusing Hegseth of waging war without congressional approval.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo draws 2.5 million in Buenos Aires, renews warning over Milei's austerity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d93df5f043f16e50f38d31c68c328bf9e2923122e294af5c4a44c73e3d8fddf4</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T18:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-draws-2-5-million-in-buenos-aires-renews-warning-over-milei-s-austerity/a-79904137--67cd35a7915b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-draws-2-5-million-in-buenos-aires-renews-warning-over-milei-s-austerity/a-79904137?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some 2.5 million people have attended Pope Leo's mass in Buenos Aires, his largest gathering yet. The pontiff once again called for protecting the vulnerable as President Milei cuts disability care and social services.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>French officials blame Iran for supermarket fridge hacking</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27986358e1b2c7fa2406d9d389726525d86b58c4a287a0243d94a418992f9a2e</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T18:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/french-officials-blame-iran-for-supermarket-fridge-hacking/a-79903646--bd5606ff5b72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/french-officials-blame-iran-for-supermarket-fridge-hacking/a-79903646?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The recent cyberattack on refrigerators and freezers in supermarkets in France was organized by Iran's Revolutionary Guards, French Foreign Minister Jean-Noel Barrot has said, describing the hacking as "unprecedented."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia: Independent Novaya Gazeta shuts its Moscow newsroom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5034fd6f9cb4679b748b156931ba5e40c20414ceb223804491eec7e1fe005b89</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-independent-novaya-gazeta-shuts-its-moscow-newsroom/a-79899827--d187f3fbc3fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-independent-novaya-gazeta-shuts-its-moscow-newsroom/a-79899827?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The investigative newspaper is closing its doors after Russian authorities labeled it a "foreign agent" and ordered it vacate its Moscow premises.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India's demonetization: 10 years on, promises remain unfulfilled</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f77e8dae84ff1cbca9745712356a7513d436f1043d33bc715bf38c960288740</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-demonetization-10-years-on-promises-remain-unfulfilled/a-79903331--9f3e44d05923.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-demonetization-10-years-on-promises-remain-unfulfilled/a-79903331?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A decade after the 2016 currency ban, its impact on India's economy and the fight against black money remains contested.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey: Norway says it's been kicked out of World Juniors in favor of Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e80783efe6c2da0d6623a95bcf8b5fbd6b41d06c22754db5dffa5a8ace5fce2f</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-norway-says-it-s-been-kicked-out-of-world-juniors-in-favor-of-russia/a-79901844--fd1320af05c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-norway-says-it-s-been-kicked-out-of-world-juniors-in-favor-of-russia/a-79901844?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The wrangling over Russia's return to international ice hockey continues, with Norway saying it has been kicked out of the next major tournament to accommodate Russia. Switzerland has joined a "boycott."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Fake news in Africa: In an age of disinformation, who decides what's true?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be3506ccc00f595c96e35d5d7b1b40a997f023178ec6e557f27db5a2c2b19793</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fake-news-in-africa-in-an-age-of-disinformation-who-decides-what-s-true/a-79874039--77395478e042.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fake-news-in-africa-in-an-age-of-disinformation-who-decides-what-s-true/a-79874039?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Ghana to Mozambique, the fight against fake news keeps gaining momentum. But combating disinformation also requires safeguards for free speech, leaving some governments in an inconvenient position.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Workers killed in Izmir steel plant blast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3635ca896313b6c51ab2db8ce890bd6c853668d7d1028a03cb308b90c0ad303c</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-workers-killed-in-izmir-steel-plant-blast/a-79900748--c2f3abf41fd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-workers-killed-in-izmir-steel-plant-blast/a-79900748?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least 16 workers lost their lives in an explosion at a steel factory in Izmir. President Recep Tayyip Erdogan issued an updated casualty toll after a Cabinet meeting.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Strait of Hormuz still a source of leverage for Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:969e470c2d50bde1f18ba644673ca0a591bfea8b7f257812e83e30a9bc5e18ce</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-still-a-source-of-leverage-for-iran/a-79901647--d567b41d9be2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-still-a-source-of-leverage-for-iran/a-79901647?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Attacks in the Strait of Hormuz put crews at risk and drive up energy shipping costs. Iran's ability to sustain them and the limits of US protection will shape how much trade can continue and at what price.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russell Brand sentenced to over 10 years in prison for rape and sexual assault convictions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3851e297cc0c832a463a57947ede198421383d4c0c71412b55fa0f8ca8c14c16</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T14:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russell-brand-sentenced-to-over-10-years-in-prison-for-rape-and-sexual-assault-convictions/a-79896124--0e13af65a2fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russell-brand-sentenced-to-over-10-years-in-prison-for-rape-and-sexual-assault-convictions/a-79896124?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The former comedian was found guilty of raping one woman and sexually assaulting three others last week. The judge referred to Brand as a "predator."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>37 years after fall of Berlin Wall: How divided are Germans?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:672666c56974f4fb40c6d38b6192a3de33277444274f92b1f74752b78daf2528</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/37-years-after-fall-of-berlin-wall-how-divided-are-germans/a-79877461--471b79fce1fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/37-years-after-fall-of-berlin-wall-how-divided-are-germans/a-79877461?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three artists share their thoughts on the reunification of East and West Germany. How do they perceive a shared "we" and what gives them cause for optimism?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: CDU names Ilse Aigner as candidate for president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85d4da8d1668e708d184668c11ef516baa862b50f2a1dcce3e93e3a984fe92ae</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T12:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-cdu-names-ilse-aigner-as-candidate-for-president/a-79898143--f4c7d81c5dcc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-cdu-names-ilse-aigner-as-candidate-for-president/a-79898143?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The steering committtee of the CDU have announced Bavarian politician Ilse Aigner as presidential candidate. This gives her a good chance of becoming the first woman to occupy the role.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU aims to pick new ECB chief by year-end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b820ea06abdc6d14f6e45cc72c6f93680aab4fef3f7ddcd2f93bbfa663fa64d</id><updated>2026-11-10T07:31:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-aims-to-pick-new-ecb-chief-by-year-end/a-79898169--04bae0a2e38e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-aims-to-pick-new-ecb-chief-by-year-end/a-79898169?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Christine Lagarde's decision to step down early as head of the European Central Bank (ECB) has put the European Union on a tight schedule. The bloc expects to pick a new ECB chief by the end of December.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
